 "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "589d7ba12e1dd64c8adb14c0668ccfde6c89b193b06b0e537a3101540f23b186"} {"question" "q-74136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-7"] ["math" "-\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1+4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-2}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "589d7ba12e1dd64c8adb14c0668ccfde6c89b193b06b0e537a3101540f23b186"} {"question" "q-39244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+0+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "589d7ba12e1dd64c8adb14c0668ccfde6c89b193b06b0e537a3101540f23b186"} {"question" "q-74147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$, if $u=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ \\frac{k}{9} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}\\end{aligned}]$ is a unit vector." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $x$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}+{(\\frac{k}{9})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+{(\\frac{8}{9})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{81}+\\frac{{k}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{64}{81}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{74+{k}^{2}}{81}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖u‖=1,$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{74+{k}^{2}}{81}} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{74+{k}^{2}} & =9 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{74+{k}^{2}})}^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ 74+{k}^{2} & =81 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =7 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "589d7ba12e1dd64c8adb14c0668ccfde6c89b193b06b0e537a3101540f23b186"} {"question" "q-39862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=\\pm 2"] ["math" "k=\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "k=\\pm 7"] ["math" "k=\\pm \\sqrt{11}"] ["math" "k=\\pm \\sqrt{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-39862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=\\pm \\sqrt{7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -k \\\\ 2k \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if the distance between the vectors is $\\text{d}(x,y)=2\\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the distance between $x$ and $y$ in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{y}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-k)^{2}+(-k-(-1))^{2}+(2k-0)^{2}+(0-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9-6k+{k}^{2}+{k}^{2}-2k+1+4{k}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $\\text{d}(x,y)=2\\sqrt{3},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14} & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14})}^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2} \\\\ 6{k}^{2}-8k+14 & =12 \\\\ 6{k}^{2}-8k+2 & =0 \\\\ 3{k}^{2}-4k+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quadratic formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(3)(1)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{4}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 2}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $k=1$ and $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "589d7ba12e1dd64c8adb14c0668ccfde6c89b193b06b0e537a3101540f23b186"} {"question" "q-74151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=1,3"] ["math" "k=1,\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "k=\\pm 1"] ["math" "k=\\pm 3"] ["math" "k=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=1,\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "589d7ba12e1dd64c8adb14c0668ccfde6c89b193b06b0e537a3101540f23b186"} {"question" "q-74138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "q-74138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f13ea6518011f995527c2cbfcbe84beaa89d5795a02cce6e033b41d0a26694f"} {"question" "e-5538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/eec8345a2a1eb622aafae6890c6548efcd5b595d18334b5bad9e43f8b0fd4534.png) find $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-5538.json" "file_sha256" "b1c9f4ee4a8cfe15f74b902be2fd778ce9b1cb58a48bef6e0686825e4e2fa5ec"} {"question" "e-5538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-5538.json" "file_sha256" "b1c9f4ee4a8cfe15f74b902be2fd778ce9b1cb58a48bef6e0686825e4e2fa5ec"} {"question" "e-5539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/c3261bc45f978551da6b9ae98489e4eeceadfb5a4669a703736b3d623ed2c41d.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/40f7e2f6c5aaff24c18d65776fbbb62f44effeb921bc6e54a4e4f7ada905e614.png) find the distance $\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-5539.json" "file_sha256" "78875a94267231c339fa3c8334808e179354956bf598182db6b36a821a051bc6"} {"question" "e-5539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the distance, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1-2)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-5539.json" "file_sha256" "78875a94267231c339fa3c8334808e179354956bf598182db6b36a821a051bc6"} {"question" "e-6190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\left\\Vert {- \\dfrac{ \\mathbf{x} }{2} } \\right\\Vert = 5,$ find $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-6190.json" "file_sha256" "5e08c7b8ec95627ab991f48c98062b1539d85466759ceb6975ae846739a9047a"} {"question" "e-6190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\\Vert k \\mathbf{x} \\Vert= \\vert k \\vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $\\Vert x \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-\\frac{x}{2}‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖-\\frac{1}{2}x‖ & =5 \\\\ |-\\frac{1}{2}|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3x‖ & =3\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-6190.json" "file_sha256" "5e08c7b8ec95627ab991f48c98062b1539d85466759ceb6975ae846739a9047a"} {"question" "e-5540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Normalize the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/33fcf438acd77616d7f5c6881234f9dcc87136575b741af6af72eee9d4401dfb.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-5540.json" "file_sha256" "b37eae37ab855efad0a0362ffd30c3e1c9be2d1870c37942141cb129e1ee3eef"} {"question" "e-5540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To normalize a vector $\\mathbf{x},$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|}.$ Therefore, to normalize $\\mathbf{x},$ we first calculate $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $\\mathbf{x}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8}{10} \\\\ \\frac{6}{10}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-5540.json" "file_sha256" "b37eae37ab855efad0a0362ffd30c3e1c9be2d1870c37942141cb129e1ee3eef"}] "usage" {"e-5540" [] "e-5539" [] "e-6190" [] "q-39238" [] "e-5538" [] "q-39212" [] "q-39244" []} "basis" 1656 "retractions" [[17592186134126 :question/problem "Given $x = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, find $‖x‖$."] [17592186134129 :question/problem "Given $a = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$, find $‖a‖$."] [17592186134132 :question/problem "Normalize the vector $x = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186133489 :question/problem "Given $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$ find $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$."] [17592186133489 :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖x‖ &= \\sqrt{x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + (-4)^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 16 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{50} \\\\\n&= 5\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133490 :question/problem "Given the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ find the distance $\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y})$."] [17592186133490 :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd(x, y) &= ‖x - y‖ \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(x_{1} - y_{1})^{2} + (x_{2} - y_{2})^{2} + (x_{3} - y_{3})^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-1 - 2)^{2} + (2 - 0)^{2} + (3 - (-1))^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-3)^{2} + 2^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 4 + 16} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{29}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133562 :question/problem "If $\\left\\Vert {-\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{2}} \\right\\Vert = 5$, find $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert$."] [17592186133562 :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\\Vert k \\mathbf{x} \\Vert= \\vert k \\vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $\\Vert x \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖- \\frac{x}{2}‖ &= 5 \\\\\n‖- \\frac{1}{2}x‖ &= 5 \\\\\n\\mid - \\frac{1}{2} \\mid \\cdot ‖x‖ &= 5 \\\\\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot ‖x‖ &= 5 \\\\\n‖x‖ &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖3x‖ &= 3 \\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 10 \\\\\n&= 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133491 :question/problem "Normalize the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186133491 :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $\\mathbf{x}$, we have to divide the vector by its norm:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to normalize $\\mathbf{x}$, we first calculate $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖x‖ &= \\sqrt{x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-8)^{2} + 6^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{64 + 36} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{100} \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $\\mathbf{x}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖} &= \\frac{x}{10} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}x \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-8}{10} \\\\ \\frac{6}{10}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186131199 17592186131200 17592186131201 17592186131202 17592186131203 17592186131217 17592186131218 17592186131219 17592186131220 17592186131221 17592186131235 17592186131236 17592186131237 17592186131238 17592186131239] "immutable_fields" [[17592186131198 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131198 :answer-field/id] [17592186131198 :answer-field/key] [17592186131198 :answer-field/type] [17592186131216 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131216 :answer-field/id] [17592186131216 :answer-field/key] [17592186131216 :answer-field/type] [17592186131234 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131234 :answer-field/id] [17592186131234 :answer-field/key] [17592186131234 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
